# RedBug Help Ver 1.0

## Introduction

### Features
**Features**

   KKC (Ketchup Killers Commander) is a dual-panel terminal file manager
   written in Rust, inspired by the classic Norton Commander interface.

   Key features:

   - Dual-panel browsing with tab support in each panel
   - Internal file viewer: Text, Hex, ANSI and Image modes
   - [File search](#search-file-s) by name and content
   - [Copy](#copy-file), [Move](#move-file), [Delete](#delete-file), [Mkdir](#create-directory), Rename
   - [Wildcard selection](#select-files) with pattern matching
   - [Directory bookmarks](#directory-bookmarks) for quick navigation
   - [Remote browsing](#remote-browsing) via SFTP and IMAP
   - [Built-in archive browsing](#commands-in-archives) (ZIP and more)
   - [Lua plugin system](#plugins) for custom viewers and file handlers
   - [File associations](#file-associations) to launch any external program
   - Hundreds of color themes
   - Configurable via [Options > Setup](#configuration)

---

