## Quick use of command

### Keyboard Summary
**Keyboard Summary**

#### Function Keys (Panel)

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| F1 | This Help. |
| F2 | Open [Menu bar](#menu-bar). |
| F3 | [View file](#view-file) (internal viewer). |
| F4 | [Edit file](#edit-file) with configured or internal editor. |
| F5 | [Copy](#copy-file) selected files to other panel. |
| F6 | [Move](#move-file) selected files to other panel. |
| F7 | [Create directory](#create-directory). |
| F8 | [Delete](#delete-file) selected files. |
| F10 | Quit KKC. |

#### Navigation

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| UP / DOWN | Move cursor up / down. |
| PGUP / PGDN | Move one page up / down. |
| HOME | Jump to first entry. |
| END | Jump to last entry. |
| TAB | Switch active panel. |
| ENTER | Enter directory or open file. |
| BACKSPACE | Go to parent directory. |

#### Selection

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| INS | Select / deselect current file. |
| SPACE | Select / deselect and move down. |
| + | [Select by wildcard pattern](#select-files). |
| - | [Deselect by wildcard pattern](#deselect-files). |
| * | [Invert selection](#inverse-selection). |

#### Quick search

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Any letter | Start quick-search: type to filter entries in real time. |
| UP/DOWN | Move between matches, ENTER to jump, ESC to cancel. |

#### Ctrl shortcuts

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| C-F1 | Sort by name. |
| C-F2 | Sort by extension. |
| C-F3 | Sort by date. |
| C-F4 | Sort by size. |
| C-F5 | No sorting (original order). |
| C-A | Open plugin action palette (Lua action plugins). |
| C-D | [Directory bookmarks](#directory-bookmarks). |
| C-F | [Remote connect](#remote-browsing) (SFTP / IMAP / SMB). |
| C-G | Append a GIF frame of the current screen to data/screen.gif. |
| C-H | Toggle display of hidden files. |
| C-N | Switch to next tab. |
| C-P | Open command palette. |
| C-R | Reload directory listing. |
| C-T | Open new tab in active panel. |
| C-U / ESC | Switch to terminal / command line. |
| C-W | Close current tab. |
| C-TAB | Switch to next tab (alternative). |

#### Alt shortcuts

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| A-F4 | Toggle file_id.diz preview panel. |
| A-F7 | [Search files](#search-file-s). |

#### Shift shortcuts

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| S-F6 | [Rename](#rename-file) current file. |

### Commands in archives
**Commands in archives**

   KKC can browse ZIP archives as if they were directories.
   Press ENTER on a supported archive file to enter it.

   Inside an archive you can:
   - Navigate the directory tree
   - View files with the internal viewer (F3)
   - Copy files out of the archive to a normal directory (F5)

   Creating or modifying archives is not supported from within the browser.

### Remote browsing
**Remote browsing (SFTP / IMAP)**

   KKC supports remote file systems via SFTP and IMAP.

#### Opening a connection

   Press Ctrl-F to open the connection panel.

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| UP/DOWN | browse saved profiles |
| Type | filter profiles by name |
| ENTER | connect to selected profile |
| F6 | edit selected profile |
| F7 | add new SFTP profile |
| F8 | add new IMAP profile |
| ESC | close panel |

#### SFTP fields

| Field | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Name | profile display name |
| Host | hostname or IP address |
| Port | SSH port (default 22) |
| User | login username |
| Password | login password (stored in profile file) |
| Remote dir | initial directory after connect |

#### IMAP fields

| Field | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Name | profile display name |
| Host | IMAP server hostname |
| Port | IMAP port (default 993) |
| User | email address / username |
| Password | password |

#### Inside a remote panel

   Navigation works the same as locally.
   File operations (view, copy out, delete, rename) are supported.
   Editing uploads the file back after the editor exits.

## Command in details

### View file
**Internal file viewer**

#### Opening

   F3 on any file opens the internal viewer.
   The viewer automatically detects the file type:

| Type | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Text | plain text or source code |
| Hex | binary or unknown format |
| Ansi | file containing ANSI escape sequences |
| Image | PNG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, WebP |

#### Navigation

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| UP / DOWN | Scroll one line up / down. |
| PGUP / PGDN | Scroll one page up / down. |
| HOME | Go to beginning of file. |
| END | Go to end of file. |
| LEFT / RIGHT | Scroll 8 columns left / right (Text mode). |
| C-LEFT / C-RIGHT | Scroll 40 columns left / right. |
| C-HOME | Scroll to column 0. |
| g | Open goto dropdown. |

| Goto key | Description |
| --- | --- |
| g | Go to line number <n>, or file start if no <n>. |
| e | Go to last line. |
| s | Go to first non-blank line. |
| n | Go to next page. |
| p | Go to previous page. |

#### Search

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| F7 or / | Open search bar. |
| n | Jump to next match. |
| N | Jump to previous match. |
| C-N | Jump to next match (alternative). |
| C-J / C-K | Open next / previous file from the active panel. |

#### Viewer menus (F-keys)

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| F2 | Toggle word wrap (Text / Ansi modes). |
| F3 | Line-feed mode: DOS (CR/LF) \| Unix (LF) \| Mac (CR) \| Mixed. |
| F4 | View mode: Text \| Binary (Hex) \| Ansi \| Image \| Plugin viewer. |
| F5 | Toggle zoom (fullscreen / windowed). |
| F6 | Pre-processing pipeline (XOR, AND, OR, NEG, ROR, ADD, Latin, Elite). |
| F8 | Encoding: Plain ASCII \| DOS CP437. |
| F9 | [Keyword mask](#mask-configuration) style: C \| Pascal \| Assembler \| Ketchup \| Off. |

#### Closing

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| ESC or F10 | Return to file panel. |

#### Default Command
   F3

### Search file(s)
**Search file(s)**

   Open: Alt-F7  or  Tools > Search

   The search panel has two input fields:

| Field | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Filename | glob pattern (e.g. *.log, report*) |
| Content | optional text to search inside files |

   Press TAB to switch between the two fields.
   Press ENTER to start the search.
   Results appear below; UP/DOWN to navigate them.
   Press ENTER on a result to jump to that file's directory.
   Press ESC to close the panel.

#### Default Command
   A-F7

### Edit file
**Edit file**

   F4 on any local file launches the editor configured in Options > Setup.
   The default editor is taken from the EDITOR environment variable
   or from the 'editor' setting in the config file.

   If the editor field is empty (editor = ""), F4 opens the selected
   local file in the [Internal editor](#internal-editor) side panel instead.

   For remote files the file is downloaded, edited locally, then
   uploaded back automatically when the external editor exits.

   When config.toml is modified and saved, KKC reloads the configuration.

#### Default Command
   F4

### Internal editor
**Internal editor**

   The internal editor is shown inside a side panel and is used by F4
   when Options > Setup > Editor is empty (editor = "").

#### Keys

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| C-S | Save file. |
| A-Z | Toggle word wrap. Wrap is off by default. |
| TAB | Leave editor focus and return to the opposite panel. |
| ESC | Close editor; asks before discarding unsaved changes. |

   With wrap off, long lines scroll horizontally to keep the cursor visible.
   With wrap on, long lines are wrapped to the panel width.

   Saving config.toml from the internal editor reloads the configuration
   immediately.

### Copy file
**Copy file**

   F5 copies the selected files (or the current file if nothing is
   selected) to the other panel's directory.

   Copy dialog fields:

| Field | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Destination | target path (editable) |
| Overwrite | overwrite existing files |
| Newer only | only copy if source is newer |
| Keep attributes | preserve timestamps and permissions |

   Navigation: Tab / Up / Down between fields.
   Space toggles checkboxes.  Enter or OK starts the copy.
   ESC cancels.

#### Default Command
   F5

### Move file
**Move file**

   F6 moves selected files to the other panel's directory.
   Same dialog as [Copy](#copy-file).

#### Default Command
   F6

### Create directory
**Create directory**

   F7 opens a name prompt. Type the new directory name and press Enter.
   ESC cancels.

#### Default Command
   F7

### Delete file
**Delete files**

   F8 deletes the selected files (or current file).
   A confirmation dialog is shown if 'Confirm delete' is enabled in
   [Options > Setup](#configuration).

#### Default Command
   F8

### Rename file
**Rename file**

   Shift-F6 opens a rename prompt pre-filled with the current filename.
   Edit and press Enter to rename.  ESC cancels.

#### Default Command
   S-F6

### Select files
**Select files by pattern**

   '+' opens a wildcard dialog.  Default pattern is '*'.
   Examples: *.txt   report_??.*

#### Default Command
   +

### Deselect files
**Deselect files by pattern**

   '-' opens a wildcard dialog to deselect matching files.

#### Default Command
   -

### Inverse selection
**Invert selection**

   '*' inverts the current selection (selected becomes unselected and
   vice versa).

#### Default Command
   *

### Directory bookmarks
**Directory bookmarks**

   Ctrl-D opens the bookmarks panel, which shows saved directory paths.

   - Type to filter bookmarks by name.
   - UP / DOWN to navigate the list.
   - ENTER to jump to the selected directory.
   - DELETE to remove the selected bookmark.
   - The first item is always "Add current directory".
   - Backspace deletes the last filter character.
   - ESC closes the panel.

#### Default Command
   C-D

### Plugins
**Lua plugin system**

   KKC supports Lua plugins that extend the viewer and file handling.

   Each plugin is a directory (or .kkplug bundle) containing:

| File | Description |
| --- | --- |
| plugin.lua | Lua script |
| plugin.toml | metadata (name, version, description) |

   Installed plugins are stored in the user data directory.
   Press Enter on a .kkplug file to install it automatically.

   Options > Plugins opens the plugin list:

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| UP / DOWN | navigate |
| ENTER / O | open plugin directory |
| ESC / F10 | close |

   Plugins can provide custom viewers that appear in the F4 viewer
   mode picker as "Plugins viewer > [plugin name]".

#### Default Command
   Options > Plugins

### File associations
**File associations**

   Options > Associations manages per-extension openers.

   For each extension you can define one or more commands.
   Use '%f' as a placeholder for the file path, or the path is
   appended automatically.

   Example:

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Extension | mp4 |
| Openers | mpv %f, vlc %f |

   If multiple openers exist for a file, a picker is shown on ENTER.

   Association editor keys:

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| A / + / F1 | Add new association |
| ENTER / E | Edit selected |
| DELETE / D | Delete selected |
| ESC | Close |

#### Default Command
   Options > Associations

## Menu

### Menu bar
**Menu bar**

   F2 (or the F2 button in the key bar) opens the menu bar.

| Menu | Entries |
| --- | --- |
| File | View, Edit, Copy, Move, Mkdir, Rename, Delete, Quit |
| Panel | Swap panels, Sort, Toggle hidden, Reload |
| Disk | Go to path |
| Selection | Select, Deselect, Invert |
| Tools | Search, Bookmarks |
| Options | Setup, Plugins, Associations, F-Key bar, Save Config |
| Help | Help, About |

   Navigation: LEFT / RIGHT between menus (wraps around).
   UP / DOWN within a menu.  ENTER or first-letter shortcut to activate.
   ESC closes the menu.

### Mask configuration
**Keyword mask (viewer)**

   In Text or Ansi viewer mode, F9 opens the mask menu:

| Style | Description |
| --- | --- |
| C Style | highlights C/C++ keywords |
| Pascal Style | highlights Pascal keywords |
| Assembler Style | highlights x86 assembler mnemonics |
| Ketchup Style | highlights a custom keyword set |
| Mask OFF | disable highlighting |

   The mask is rendered as bold text on the current line.

### Configuration
**Configuration (Options > Setup)**

   Setup is split into tabs. Use LEFT / RIGHT, PAGEUP / PAGEDOWN,
   ALT-LEFT / ALT-RIGHT or CTRL-LEFT / CTRL-RIGHT to switch tab.
   Use UP / DOWN or TAB / SHIFT-TAB to move inside the active tab.

#### Checkboxes

| Option | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Confirm exit | Ask before quitting KKC. |
| Confirm delete | Ask before deleting files. |
| Auto reload | Reload panel after file operations. |
| Insert moves down | Cursor moves down after pressing Insert. |
| Select directories | Include directories in wildcard selection. |
| Show hidden files | Display hidden / dot files. |
| Color by type | Color entries by file type / extension. |
| Cloud icons | Show a cloud icon for files available only online. |
| File icons | Show folder and file-type icons in panels. |
| Show F-key bar | Display the function-key shortcut bar. |

#### Text fields

| Field | Description |
| --- | --- |
| Editor | Command to launch for F4 (e.g. nano, vim, code). |
| Pager | Command for viewing large text files. |
| Dir history max | Maximum number of entries in directory bookmarks. |

   Leave empty to use the internal editor for local files.

#### Buttons

| Shortcut | Description |
| --- | --- |
| OK / Enter | Apply and save configuration. |
| Cancel / ESC | Discard changes. |

## Miscellaneous

### About KKC
**About KKC**

   KKC - Ketchup Killers Commander
   Rust rewrite by [RedBug](#contact) (Miguel Vanhove)

   Originally created in 1997 as a DOS file manager.
   This version is a complete rewrite in Rust using the ratatui TUI library.

   Source code and releases:
   https://github.com/redbug26/kkc-rust

   Report bugs and ideas via GitHub Issues.

### Contact
**How to contact me ?**

   GitHub : https://github.com/redbug26
   Issues : https://github.com/redbug26/kkc-rust/issues

### History
**History**

  V0.1.18
   - Error/status messages now displayed in a proper dialog box
   - Tab support: multiple tabs per panel, tabs saved and restored
   across sessions
   - Viewer optimisation: faster rendering, viewer split into
   sub-modules (events/viewer.rs, ui/panel.rs)
   - CSV viewer: word-wrap support for long cells
   - XML viewer plugin added
   - MIME type detection used throughout (plugins, archive, idf)
   - IDF/file-ID probing extended: many more formats recognised
   in the status bar (modules, samples, pictures, animations)
   - Amstrad CPC & C64 Disk plugin: improved directory listing
   - Viewer highlight submenu: new sub-menu to control syntax/keyword
   highlighting; viewer events and UI refactored into separate files
   - Panels refactored into ui/panel.rs
   - FileID panel improvment

  V0.1.17
   - Complete rewrite in Rust using ratatui + crossterm
   - Dual-panel TUI with tab support in each panel
   - Internal viewer: Text / Hex / Ansi / Image modes (lazy decoding)
   - Archive browsing (ZIP)
   - Remote browsing: SFTP and IMAP
   - Lua plugin system with viewer plugins
   - File associations with multi-opener picker
   - Directory bookmarks with fuzzy filter
   - File search by name and content
   - macOS/linux Homebrew distribution

  2026 - Rust rewrite

